      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the local Richland Baptist Church, itself named after Richland, South Carolina, where many early settlers originated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richland%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Richland lies along U.S. Route 280 and Georgia State Route 520, with those highways connecting it northwest to Columbus and southeast to Albany.",
